From 431985ccfc8bd2de1c9cff4c0416213be288c3e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 01:46:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93 - restore four-byte SG offset validation

Removing the SG offset check still causes intermittent device failures
with the 64-byte input and output thresholds. The direct test reported
an ECB-DES encryption mismatch in the final eight bytes of a 16368-byte
request using the byte-offset layout (seed 1708171853, case 322).

That layout uses a single source SG entry at allocation offset 129 and a
separate destination at offset 131. The destination is already bounced
for cache-line isolation, while the source is no longer bounced. ECB
does not use an IV, counter or authentication tag.

Revert patch 028 and restore the four-byte SG start-offset check. The
lower DMA thresholds are insufficient to make unaligned sources safe
on the tested device. Keep the 64-byte thresholds and native authenc
packet-tag path; the prepared driver again matches release 20, which
passed the full device test matrix with three repetitions.

Signed-off-by: LGA1150 <9155358+LGA1150@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 eip93-common.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/eip93-common.c b/eip93-common.c
index 8c42282..8850fc3 100644
--- a/eip93-common.c
+++ b/eip93-common.c
@@ -262,8 +262,12 @@ static bool eip93_is_sg_aligned(struct scatterlist *sg, u32 len,
 	int nents;
 
 	for (nents = 0; sg; sg = sg_next(sg), ++nents) {
+		if (!IS_ALIGNED(sg->offset, 4))
+			return false;
+
 		/*
 		 * DMA-written buffers must not share cache lines with CPU writes.
+		 * Read-only sources only need the hardware alignment checks.
 		 * dma_map_sg() maps the entire entry, including any bytes beyond
 		 * the requested crypt length in the last entry.
 		 */
-- 
